On Azure, images are stored under resource-group and made available under
resource-group-->image-gallery-->image-definition.  We need to make sure
these are available before running the packer file to create the image.
Unless it is a new env, resource-group and image-gallery should have been
created.  By default, they are named "image-factory" and "capella" respectly.
New image-definition are created for each release, i.e.
"couchbase-serverless-server-7.5.0" and "couchbase-serverless-backup-7.5.0".

To verify these, run:
  * az login --service-principal -u <client_id> -p <client_pw> --tenant <tenant_id>
  * az sig list --resource-group image-factory
  * az sig image-definition list --gallery-name capella --resource-group image-factory

To create new image-definitions:
  *   az sig image-definition create --gallery-image-definition couchbase-serverless-server-7.5.0 \
    --gallery-name capella \
    --offer server \
    --os-type Linux \
    --publisher couchbase-capella \
    --resource-group image-factory \
    --hyper-v-generation v2 \
    --sku couchbase-serverless-server-7.5.0

  *   az sig image-definition create --gallery-image-definition couchbase-serverless-backup-7.5.0 \
    --gallery-name capella \
    --offer backup \
    --os-type Linux \
    --publisher couchbase-capella \
    --resource-group image-factory \
    --hyper-v-generation v2 \
    --sku couchbase-serverless-backup-7.5.0

To publish a new image:
  * create .env based on .env.example
  * source .env
  * packer init couchbase-server.pkr.hcl
  * packer build couchbase-server.pkr.hcl


Other useful az commands:
  * To delete an image:
    az image delete --name couchbase-cloud-server-7.1.3-3480 --resource-group image-factory
  * To delete an image version:
    az sig image-version delete --gallery-image-version 1.0.3480  --resource-group image-factory --gallery-name capella --gallery-image-definition couchbase-cloud-server-7.1.3
  * To delete an image definition:
    az sig image-definition delete --resource-group image-factory --gallery-name capella --gallery-image-definition couchbase-cloud-server-7.1.3
  * To create a VM:
    get image id by running "az image show --name couchbase-cloud-server-7.1.3-3480 --resource-group image-factory"
    az vm create --resource-group image-factory --name mings-vm --image <image id from command above> --admin-username azureuser --generate-ssh-keys
    Note: public ssh key is generated based on ~/.ssh/id_rsa and is stored on Azure.  ~/.ssh/id_rsa is created if it doesn't exist.
  * To delete a VM:
    az vm delete --resource-group image-factory --name mings-vm
